1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
Today's Video: How to Ask for a Day Off

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Basic Japanese Greetings and Seat Confirmation

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:13,474
Excuse me.

4
00:00:13,497 --> 00:00:14,542
Yes?

5
00:00:14,566 --> 00:00:17,099
Is this seat taken?

6
00:00:17,122 --> 00:00:18,922
Oh, no, it's free.

7
00:00:18,945 --> 00:00:21,545
Mind if I sit here?

8
00:00:21,568 --> 00:00:22,935
Go ahead.

9
00:00:22,958 --> 00:00:24,811
Thanks!

10
00:00:24,835 --> 00:00:26,635
No problem.

11
00:00:26,658 --> 00:00:28,891
You have a lot of luggage.

12
00:00:28,914 --> 00:00:30,720
Excuse me.

13
00:00:30,744 --> 00:00:32,744
It's fine, really.

14
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:35,460
I'll just move it a bit.

15
00:00:35,484 --> 00:00:37,017
Excuse me.

16
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,773
Don't worry about it.

17
00:00:38,796 --> 00:00:40,286
Going on a trip?

18
00:00:40,309 --> 00:00:41,686
Yes?

19
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:43,876
Where to?

20
00:00:43,899 --> 00:00:45,899
Tokyo.

21
00:00:45,922 --> 00:00:47,557
Nice!

22
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:49,059
Yes?

23
00:00:49,083 --> 00:00:50,816
For sightseeing?

24
00:00:50,839 --> 00:00:52,486
That's right.

25
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:55,114
I'm here for work.

26
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:56,998
Hope it goes well for you.

27
00:00:57,021 --> 00:00:58,754
Thanks!

28
00:00:58,777 --> 00:01:01,178
How many days are you staying?

29
00:01:01,201 --> 00:01:02,968
Three days.

30
00:01:02,992 --> 00:01:04,838
That's a long trip.

31
00:01:04,861 --> 00:01:06,228
Go ahead.

32
00:01:06,251 --> 00:01:08,738
Take care, okay?

33
00:01:08,762 --> 00:01:17,771
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

34
00:01:17,771 --> 00:01:19,271
Scene 2: Greetings and Cherry Blossom Photography

35
00:01:19,271 --> 00:01:21,404
Excuse me.

36
00:01:21,427 --> 00:01:22,904
Yes?

37
00:01:22,927 --> 00:01:25,861
Is it okay if I take a photo?

38
00:01:25,884 --> 00:01:28,017
Here?

39
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:29,814
Yes?

40
00:01:29,838 --> 00:01:31,916
Sure, go ahead.

41
00:01:31,939 --> 00:01:34,183
Thanks!

42
00:01:34,207 --> 00:01:36,862
What are you taking a picture of?

43
00:01:36,885 --> 00:01:39,419
Those flowers over there.

44
00:01:39,442 --> 00:01:41,661
They're beautiful.

45
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:43,660
Go ahead.

46
00:01:43,683 --> 00:01:45,916
Are those cherry blossoms?

47
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:48,075
That's right.

48
00:01:48,099 --> 00:01:50,667
They're already blooming.

49
00:01:50,690 --> 00:01:53,548
It's warm, so they are.

50
00:01:53,572 --> 00:01:55,658
Yeah, it is.

51
00:01:55,681 --> 00:01:58,448
I come here every year.

52
00:01:58,471 --> 00:02:00,837
Really?

53
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:02,506
Yes?

54
00:02:02,529 --> 00:02:05,330
This is my first time.

55
00:02:05,354 --> 00:02:08,043
It's a great spot.

56
00:02:08,066 --> 00:02:10,699
Can I see the photo?

57
00:02:10,722 --> 00:02:13,089
Sure, go ahead.

58
00:02:13,112 --> 00:02:15,512
Wow, that's amazing!

59
00:02:15,535 --> 00:02:18,302
It's a good camera.

60
00:02:18,325 --> 00:02:20,760
You take photos like a pro!

61
00:02:20,783 --> 00:02:23,358
Oh, not at all.

62
00:02:23,382 --> 00:02:26,868
I want a camera too.

63
00:02:26,891 --> 00:02:29,091
It's a lot of fun.

64
00:02:29,114 --> 00:02:31,581
I'll look into it.

65
00:02:31,604 --> 00:02:38,709
You can find the link to review today's video in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without prior notice.

66
00:02:38,709 --> 00:02:40,209
Scene 3: Borrowing a Pen

67
00:02:40,209 --> 00:02:41,776
Hey.

68
00:02:41,799 --> 00:02:42,936
Yeah?

69
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:46,213
Can I borrow a pen for a sec?

70
00:02:46,237 --> 00:02:47,570
Sure.

71
00:02:47,593 --> 00:02:49,004
Thanks.

72
00:02:49,027 --> 00:02:51,436
I’ve got red and black.

73
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:53,260
Black, please.

74
00:02:53,284 --> 00:02:54,684
Yes?

75
00:02:54,707 --> 00:02:56,521
You’re a lifesaver.

76
00:02:56,544 --> 00:02:58,378
What are you writing?

77
00:02:58,401 --> 00:03:00,251
Just a note.

78
00:03:00,274 --> 00:03:01,849
Ah, got it.

79
00:03:01,872 --> 00:03:04,306
I’m jotting down a phone number.

80
00:03:04,329 --> 00:03:06,583
Whose number?

81
00:03:06,607 --> 00:03:08,540
A friend’s.

82
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:10,050
Meeting up?

83
00:03:10,074 --> 00:03:11,248
Yep.

84
00:03:11,271 --> 00:03:13,008
When?

85
00:03:13,032 --> 00:03:14,799
Tomorrow.

86
00:03:14,822 --> 00:03:16,099
Where?

87
00:03:16,122 --> 00:03:18,357
In front of the station.

88
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:19,863
Nice.

89
00:03:19,887 --> 00:03:22,020
We’re watching a movie.

90
00:03:22,043 --> 00:03:23,678
What kind?

91
00:03:23,701 --> 00:03:25,901
An anime.

92
00:03:25,924 --> 00:03:28,124
Sounds fun.

93
00:03:28,147 --> 00:03:30,616
I’ve been wanting to see it for ages.

94
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:32,607
Have a great time!

95
00:03:32,630 --> 00:03:34,468
Here’s your pen back.

96
00:03:34,492 --> 00:03:36,125
Thanks.

97
00:03:36,148 --> 00:03:37,648
Scene 4: Toothache and Leaving Work Early

98
00:03:37,648 --> 00:03:39,281
Manager.

99
00:03:39,304 --> 00:03:40,744
Yes?

100
00:03:40,768 --> 00:03:42,809
Hope it goes well for you.

101
00:03:42,832 --> 00:03:44,972
Good work today.

102
00:03:44,995 --> 00:03:49,795
Could I leave a little early today?

103
00:03:49,818 --> 00:03:52,113
What’s up?

104
00:03:52,137 --> 00:03:54,418
I need to go to the hospital.

105
00:03:54,441 --> 00:03:57,696
Are you feeling unwell?

106
00:03:57,719 --> 00:04:00,600
No, it’s the dentist.

107
00:04:00,624 --> 00:04:03,590
Toothache?

108
00:04:03,613 --> 00:04:04,901
Yes?

109
00:04:04,924 --> 00:04:08,291
That’s rough.

110
00:04:08,314 --> 00:04:09,748
Excuse me.

111
00:04:09,771 --> 00:04:12,905
What time are you leaving?

112
00:04:12,929 --> 00:04:14,929
Would 3 PM work?

113
00:04:14,952 --> 00:04:17,407
Sure, go ahead.

114
00:04:17,430 --> 00:04:19,430
Thanks!

115
00:04:19,453 --> 00:04:22,537
Finished your work?

116
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,008
Yes?

117
00:04:24,032 --> 00:04:26,965
Did you complete the documents?

118
00:04:26,988 --> 00:04:29,588
They’re on my desk.

119
00:04:29,611 --> 00:04:31,745
Understood.

120
00:04:31,768 --> 00:04:34,601
I’ll be in as usual tomorrow.

121
00:04:34,624 --> 00:04:36,758
Take it easy.

122
00:04:36,781 --> 00:04:39,348
Thanks!

123
00:04:39,371 --> 00:04:41,204
Take care.

124
00:04:41,227 --> 00:04:43,394
Excuse me.

125
00:04:43,417 --> 00:04:45,383
Good work today.

126
00:04:45,406 --> 00:04:46,906
Scene 5: Adjusting the Temperature in Conversation

127
00:04:46,906 --> 00:04:48,640
Hey.

128
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:49,996
Yep.

129
00:04:50,019 --> 00:04:53,263
Can I turn down the AC a bit?

130
00:04:53,286 --> 00:04:55,297
Are you cold?

131
00:04:55,321 --> 00:04:58,254
A little, yeah.

132
00:04:58,277 --> 00:04:59,882
Sure.

133
00:04:59,905 --> 00:05:01,472
Thanks.

134
00:05:01,495 --> 00:05:04,307
The remote’s right there.

135
00:05:04,330 --> 00:05:06,145
Got it.

136
00:05:06,168 --> 00:05:08,002
What temperature should I set it to?

137
00:05:08,025 --> 00:05:10,858
Twenty-six degrees is fine.

138
00:05:10,881 --> 00:05:12,414
Sure.

139
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:15,209
I’ll lower the fan speed too.

140
00:05:15,233 --> 00:05:16,730
Got it.

141
00:05:16,753 --> 00:05:18,572
Sorry about that.

142
00:05:18,595 --> 00:05:21,129
It’s totally fine.

143
00:05:21,152 --> 00:05:23,435
It’s hot outside, huh?

144
00:05:23,459 --> 00:05:26,031
So hot.

145
00:05:26,054 --> 00:05:28,723
It’s summer, after all.

146
00:05:28,746 --> 00:05:29,961
Yep.

147
00:05:29,985 --> 00:05:32,027
Want some ice cream?

148
00:05:32,051 --> 00:05:33,830
Yeah, I’ll have some.

149
00:05:33,853 --> 00:05:36,187
It’s in the fridge.

150
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:37,826
I’ll grab it.

151
00:05:37,849 --> 00:05:39,334
Thanks.

152
00:05:39,357 --> 00:05:41,091
Is chocolate okay?

153
00:05:41,114 --> 00:05:42,780
Yep.

154
00:05:42,803 --> 00:05:44,672
Here you go.

155
00:05:44,696 --> 00:05:46,163
Thanks.

156
00:05:46,186 --> 00:05:48,586
This is good.

157
00:05:48,608 --> 00:05:50,108
Scene 6: Trying on Clothes Conversation

158
00:05:50,108 --> 00:05:52,042
Excuse me.

159
00:05:52,065 --> 00:05:53,265
Yes?

160
00:05:53,288 --> 00:05:56,821
Can I try this on?

161
00:05:56,844 --> 00:05:58,977
Of course.

162
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,767
Where are the fitting rooms?

163
00:06:00,790 --> 00:06:03,190
Right over there.

164
00:06:03,213 --> 00:06:05,213
Thanks!

165
00:06:05,236 --> 00:06:08,049
How’s the size?

166
00:06:08,073 --> 00:06:11,139
It’s a little big.

167
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:14,008
I’ll bring you a smaller size.

168
00:06:14,032 --> 00:06:16,087
Please do.

169
00:06:16,110 --> 00:06:18,076
Here you go.

170
00:06:18,099 --> 00:06:19,899
Thanks!

171
00:06:19,922 --> 00:06:21,756
How does it fit?

172
00:06:21,779 --> 00:06:24,425
It’s perfect.

173
00:06:24,448 --> 00:06:26,482
Great!

174
00:06:26,505 --> 00:06:29,796
Do you have this in other colors?

175
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:32,511
We have it in black and white.

176
00:06:32,534 --> 00:06:35,101
Can I see the black one?

177
00:06:35,124 --> 00:06:37,378
Certainly.

178
00:06:37,401 --> 00:06:40,212
Which one do you prefer?

179
00:06:40,236 --> 00:06:43,644
Black really suits you.

180
00:06:43,668 --> 00:06:45,635
You think so?

181
00:06:45,658 --> 00:06:47,191
Yes?

182
00:06:47,214 --> 00:06:50,024
I’ll go with the black one, then.

183
00:06:50,047 --> 00:06:51,814
Thanks!

184
00:06:51,837 --> 00:06:54,890
Can I pay with a credit card?

185
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:56,480
Yes?

186
00:06:56,503 --> 00:06:58,137
Please do.

187
00:06:58,160 --> 00:07:00,760
Certainly.

188
00:07:00,783 --> 00:07:02,283
Scene 7: Checking the Document Together

189
00:07:02,283 --> 00:07:04,449
Um...

190
00:07:04,472 --> 00:07:05,606
Yes?

191
00:07:05,629 --> 00:07:09,195
Can I take a look at that document?

192
00:07:09,218 --> 00:07:11,385
This one?

193
00:07:11,408 --> 00:07:13,241
Yep.

194
00:07:13,264 --> 00:07:15,031
Here you go.

195
00:07:15,054 --> 00:07:16,667
Thanks.

196
00:07:16,691 --> 00:07:19,626
It's tough, isn't it?

197
00:07:19,649 --> 00:07:22,449
Really tough.

198
00:07:22,472 --> 00:07:25,159
What part don’t you understand?

199
00:07:25,183 --> 00:07:27,783
It’s this number.

200
00:07:27,806 --> 00:07:30,572
Oh, that one?

201
00:07:30,595 --> 00:07:33,003
Isn’t that wrong?

202
00:07:33,027 --> 00:07:35,594
Let me check.

203
00:07:35,617 --> 00:07:37,284
Thanks.

204
00:07:37,306 --> 00:07:39,706
You’re right.

205
00:07:39,729 --> 00:07:43,704
My bad, that was my mistake.

206
00:07:43,728 --> 00:07:46,094
Please fix it.

207
00:07:46,117 --> 00:07:47,524
Yes?

208
00:07:47,548 --> 00:07:50,681
The meeting starts at three.

209
00:07:50,704 --> 00:07:52,671
I’ll make it in time.

210
00:07:52,694 --> 00:07:55,364
Could you also make copies?

211
00:07:55,387 --> 00:07:57,164
How many copies?

212
00:07:57,188 --> 00:07:59,456
Ten copies.

213
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:01,082
Got it.

214
00:08:01,106 --> 00:08:03,339
Thanks, I’m counting on you.

215
00:08:03,362 --> 00:08:04,896
Yes?

216
00:08:04,919 --> 00:08:06,375
No problem.

217
00:08:06,398 --> 00:08:08,864
I’ll do it right away.

218
00:08:08,887 --> 00:08:10,387
Scene 8: Requesting a Day Off

219
00:08:10,387 --> 00:08:12,075
Manager.

220
00:08:12,099 --> 00:08:13,533
Yes?

221
00:08:13,556 --> 00:08:17,089
Do you have a moment now?

222
00:08:17,112 --> 00:08:18,969
What’s up?

223
00:08:18,993 --> 00:08:23,826
Would it be possible to take tomorrow off?

224
00:08:23,849 --> 00:08:25,583
Tomorrow?

225
00:08:25,606 --> 00:08:27,103
Yes?

226
00:08:27,126 --> 00:08:29,359
Is something going on?

227
00:08:29,382 --> 00:08:32,235
My family member has a fever.

228
00:08:32,258 --> 00:08:34,992
That’s worrying.

229
00:08:35,015 --> 00:08:38,348
I need to take them to the hospital.

230
00:08:38,371 --> 00:08:40,038
Understood.

231
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:42,337
I’m sorry about this.

232
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,694
Don’t worry about it.

233
00:08:44,717 --> 00:08:46,717
Thanks!

234
00:08:46,740 --> 00:08:49,997
Do you have any work that needs handing over?

235
00:08:50,021 --> 00:08:53,026
I’ve asked Tanaka to cover for me.

236
00:08:53,049 --> 00:08:54,928
Understood.

237
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:57,318
I’ll check my emails too.

238
00:08:57,341 --> 00:08:59,821
Don’t push yourself too hard.

239
00:08:59,845 --> 00:09:01,678
Excuse me.

240
00:09:01,701 --> 00:09:03,435
Take care.

241
00:09:03,458 --> 00:09:04,917
Yes?

242
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:07,674
Will you be able to come the day after tomorrow?

243
00:09:07,697 --> 00:09:09,030
Yes?

244
00:09:09,053 --> 00:09:10,932
Understood.

245
00:09:10,955 --> 00:09:13,236
Thank you for your understanding.

246
00:09:13,259 --> 00:09:14,693
Yes?

247
00:09:14,716 --> 00:09:16,404
Excuse me.

248
00:09:16,428 --> 00:09:17,861
Good work today.

249
00:09:17,884 --> 00:09:19,384
Scene 9: Learning Japanese Through Conversations

250
00:09:19,384 --> 00:09:21,274
Hey.

251
00:09:21,298 --> 00:09:22,300
What?

252
00:09:22,323 --> 00:09:26,018
Can I use your charger?

253
00:09:26,042 --> 00:09:28,008
For your phone?

254
00:09:28,031 --> 00:09:29,720
Yep.

255
00:09:29,744 --> 00:09:31,555
Sure.

256
00:09:31,578 --> 00:09:33,312
Thanks.

257
00:09:33,335 --> 00:09:35,308
My battery’s dead.

258
00:09:35,331 --> 00:09:38,780
I only have one percent left!

259
00:09:38,803 --> 00:09:41,003
That’s risky.

260
00:09:41,026 --> 00:09:44,236
I was playing games the whole time.

261
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:46,027
What game?

262
00:09:46,050 --> 00:09:48,683
A puzzle game.

263
00:09:48,706 --> 00:09:50,706
Sounds fun.

264
00:09:50,729 --> 00:09:53,415
It’s *so* fun.

265
00:09:53,439 --> 00:09:55,537
Show me later.

266
00:09:55,561 --> 00:09:57,531
Sure.

267
00:09:57,554 --> 00:10:00,407
The cable’s right there.

268
00:10:00,430 --> 00:10:02,007
It won't reach.

269
00:10:02,031 --> 00:10:04,398
Come here.

270
00:10:04,421 --> 00:10:05,902
Yep.

271
00:10:05,925 --> 00:10:07,359
Got it in.

272
00:10:07,382 --> 00:10:09,589
I got it in!

273
00:10:09,612 --> 00:10:11,298
Great.

274
00:10:11,321 --> 00:10:13,288
You saved me.

275
00:10:13,312 --> 00:10:15,645
You're welcome.

276
00:10:15,668 --> 00:10:18,234
I'll give it back when I'm done.

277
00:10:18,257 --> 00:10:20,341
Take your time.

278
00:10:20,365 --> 00:10:22,332
You're so kind.

279
00:10:22,355 --> 00:10:24,688
Just normal.

280
00:10:24,711 --> 00:10:26,211
Scene 10: Greetings and Introducing a Dog

281
00:10:26,211 --> 00:10:28,378
Wow.

282
00:10:28,401 --> 00:10:30,047
Hello.

283
00:10:30,071 --> 00:10:31,926
Hello.

284
00:10:31,950 --> 00:10:34,554
Lovely weather, isn't it?

285
00:10:34,577 --> 00:10:36,673
Yes?

286
00:10:36,697 --> 00:10:40,830
Is it okay if I pet your dog?

287
00:10:40,853 --> 00:10:43,387
It's fine, really.

288
00:10:43,410 --> 00:10:45,643
Thanks!

289
00:10:45,666 --> 00:10:48,999
Don't worry, she doesn't bite.

290
00:10:49,022 --> 00:10:51,756
So cute!

291
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:53,752
Thanks!

292
00:10:53,776 --> 00:10:56,142
How old is she?

293
00:10:56,165 --> 00:10:58,419
She's three.

294
00:10:58,443 --> 00:11:00,576
Is she a boy?

295
00:11:00,599 --> 00:11:02,818
No, she's a girl.

296
00:11:02,841 --> 00:11:05,408
What's her name?

297
00:11:05,431 --> 00:11:07,264
Momo.

298
00:11:07,287 --> 00:11:09,454
Momo-chan?

299
00:11:09,477 --> 00:11:11,046
Yes?

300
00:11:11,069 --> 00:11:13,703
Her fur is so fluffy!

301
00:11:13,726 --> 00:11:16,945
I gave her a bath yesterday.

302
00:11:16,968 --> 00:11:19,535
She smells nice.

303
00:11:19,558 --> 00:11:22,332
I switched shampoos.

304
00:11:22,356 --> 00:11:25,038
She's very calm.

305
00:11:25,062 --> 00:11:27,662
She loves people.

306
00:11:27,685 --> 00:11:30,327
She's wagging her tail!

307
00:11:30,350 --> 00:11:32,717
I think she's happy.

308
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:35,196
She's so healing.

309
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:37,087
I'm glad.

310
00:11:37,110 --> 00:11:39,043
Thank you so much.

311
00:11:39,066 --> 00:11:41,667
No problem, come again!

312
00:11:51,698 --> 00:11:53,198
Scene 11: Summer Conversations

313
00:11:53,198 --> 00:11:55,565
It's hot.

314
00:11:55,588 --> 00:11:58,231
It sure is hot.

315
00:11:58,255 --> 00:12:01,945
Mind if I open the window?

316
00:12:01,968 --> 00:12:03,983
Sure, go ahead.

317
00:12:04,007 --> 00:12:05,640
Thanks.

318
00:12:05,663 --> 00:12:08,530
There's a breeze.

319
00:12:08,553 --> 00:12:10,953
Feels nice.

320
00:12:10,976 --> 00:12:12,858
Yeah, it is.

321
00:12:12,881 --> 00:12:16,419
No need for AC.

322
00:12:16,443 --> 00:12:19,290
Still manageable.

323
00:12:19,313 --> 00:12:22,446
Summer's almost here.

324
00:12:22,469 --> 00:12:24,722
Ugh, I hate it.

325
00:12:24,746 --> 00:12:27,997
Not a fan of the heat?

326
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:30,358
I really can't stand it.

327
00:12:30,381 --> 00:12:33,348
I love it.

328
00:12:33,371 --> 00:12:35,371
Heading to the beach?

329
00:12:35,394 --> 00:12:37,794
I go all the time.

330
00:12:37,817 --> 00:12:39,417
Nice!

331
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:42,040
I'll be going this year too.

332
00:12:42,063 --> 00:12:44,597
Where to?

333
00:12:44,619 --> 00:12:46,153
Okinawa.

334
00:12:46,176 --> 00:12:48,642
I'm so jealous!

335
00:12:48,665 --> 00:12:50,540
Wanna come with me?

336
00:12:50,564 --> 00:12:53,457
I don't have any time off.

337
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,352
That's too bad.

338
00:12:55,376 --> 00:12:56,976
Yes?

339
00:12:56,999 --> 00:12:59,199
I'll grab some souvenirs for you.

340
00:12:59,222 --> 00:13:01,036
Thanks!

341
00:13:01,059 --> 00:13:03,659
Can't wait!

342
00:13:03,682 --> 00:13:05,216
Yes?

343
00:13:05,239 --> 00:13:06,739
Scene 12: Ordering Conversation

344
00:13:06,739 --> 00:13:09,705
They're not here yet, huh?

345
00:13:09,728 --> 00:13:11,862
They're running late.

346
00:13:11,885 --> 00:13:15,485
Mind if I go ahead and order?

347
00:13:15,508 --> 00:13:17,741
Let's do that.

348
00:13:17,764 --> 00:13:19,967
Excuse me.

349
00:13:19,990 --> 00:13:22,806
The server's here.

350
00:13:22,830 --> 00:13:25,067
We're ready to order.

351
00:13:25,090 --> 00:13:26,667
Yes?

352
00:13:26,690 --> 00:13:28,532
What are you drinking?

353
00:13:28,555 --> 00:13:31,610
I'll have oolong tea.

354
00:13:31,634 --> 00:13:35,933
One beer and one oolong tea, please.

355
00:13:35,956 --> 00:13:38,031
Thanks!

356
00:13:38,054 --> 00:13:40,626
What about food?

357
00:13:40,650 --> 00:13:43,528
Let's get edamame.

358
00:13:43,552 --> 00:13:47,726
Edamame and some fried chicken too.

359
00:13:47,749 --> 00:13:49,916
I'd like a salad as well.

360
00:13:49,939 --> 00:13:52,139
Caesar salad okay?

361
00:13:52,162 --> 00:13:53,929
Yes?

362
00:13:53,952 --> 00:13:57,952
And an assorted yakitori platter.

363
00:13:57,975 --> 00:14:00,231
That should be enough.

364
00:14:00,254 --> 00:14:02,730
That's all for now.

365
00:14:02,754 --> 00:14:06,187
Tanaka's late, isn't he?

366
00:14:06,210 --> 00:14:09,049
Should I give him a call?

367
00:14:09,073 --> 00:14:10,673
Yeah, it is.

368
00:14:10,696 --> 00:14:13,374
Oh, looks like he's here.

369
00:14:13,397 --> 00:14:15,397
You’re right.

370
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:17,787
Good work today.

371
00:14:17,810 --> 00:14:19,976
Over here!

372
00:14:19,999 --> 00:14:22,599
We already ordered.

373
00:14:22,622 --> 00:14:24,875
We can add more.

374
00:14:24,899 --> 00:14:26,399
Scene 13: Preparing for a Meeting

375
00:14:26,399 --> 00:14:29,041
Um...

376
00:14:29,064 --> 00:14:32,798
Is it okay if we use this space?

377
00:14:32,821 --> 00:14:35,054
Starting now?

378
00:14:35,077 --> 00:14:36,644
Yes?

379
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:39,243
We're all done here.

380
00:14:39,266 --> 00:14:40,907
Really?

381
00:14:40,930 --> 00:14:43,902
I'll clean up.

382
00:14:43,926 --> 00:14:45,893
Thanks!

383
00:14:45,916 --> 00:14:48,482
Is the next group having a meeting?

384
00:14:48,505 --> 00:14:50,772
Yes, that's right.

385
00:14:50,796 --> 00:14:52,596
How many people?

386
00:14:52,619 --> 00:14:54,619
Five.

387
00:14:54,642 --> 00:14:56,975
Do we have enough chairs?

388
00:14:56,998 --> 00:14:59,077
I think we do.

389
00:14:59,101 --> 00:15:01,635
Will you be using the whiteboard?

390
00:15:01,658 --> 00:15:03,858
Yes, we will.

391
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:05,916
I'll erase it for you.

392
00:15:05,939 --> 00:15:07,946
Excuse me.

393
00:15:07,970 --> 00:15:11,503
We'll also be using the projector.

394
00:15:11,526 --> 00:15:14,259
I'll leave it as is.

395
00:15:14,282 --> 00:15:15,816
That helps a lot.

396
00:15:15,839 --> 00:15:18,473
Did you forget anything?

397
00:15:18,496 --> 00:15:21,029
There's a pen on the floor.

398
00:15:21,052 --> 00:15:23,511
Oh, that's mine.

399
00:15:23,535 --> 00:15:25,535
Here you go.

400
00:15:25,558 --> 00:15:27,171
Thanks!

401
00:15:27,194 --> 00:15:29,435
Thanks for your hard work.

402
00:15:29,458 --> 00:15:31,674
Thanks for your hard work.

403
00:15:31,698 --> 00:15:33,198
Scene 14: The Basics of Garbage Sorting

404
00:15:33,198 --> 00:15:34,835
Excuse me.

405
00:15:34,858 --> 00:15:36,105
Yes?

406
00:15:36,129 --> 00:15:39,662
Can I throw this here?

407
00:15:39,685 --> 00:15:42,119
Is this plastic?

408
00:15:42,143 --> 00:15:43,555
Yes?

409
00:15:43,578 --> 00:15:45,821
Please put it over here.

410
00:15:45,845 --> 00:15:47,898
Thanks!

411
00:15:47,921 --> 00:15:50,921
The sorting rules are strict.

412
00:15:50,944 --> 00:15:52,944
I see.

413
00:15:52,967 --> 00:15:56,065
Burnable trash goes over there.

414
00:15:56,088 --> 00:15:57,821
Understood.

415
00:15:57,844 --> 00:16:00,819
Cans and bottles go outside.

416
00:16:00,842 --> 00:16:02,576
Outside, right?

417
00:16:02,599 --> 00:16:03,932
Yes?

418
00:16:03,955 --> 00:16:05,155
Yes?

419
00:16:05,178 --> 00:16:07,752
Is it collected every day?

420
00:16:07,776 --> 00:16:11,053
No, only on Tuesdays and Fridays.

421
00:16:11,077 --> 00:16:12,710
Got it.

422
00:16:12,733 --> 00:16:16,166
Today is burnable trash day.

423
00:16:16,189 --> 00:16:17,723
You've been a big help.

424
00:16:17,746 --> 00:16:20,912
Did you just move in recently?

425
00:16:20,935 --> 00:16:22,169
Yes?

426
00:16:22,192 --> 00:16:23,841
Last week.

427
00:16:23,864 --> 00:16:25,630
Got it.

428
00:16:25,653 --> 00:16:28,420
I'm still figuring things out.

429
00:16:28,443 --> 00:16:30,843
Feel free to ask anytime.

430
00:16:30,866 --> 00:16:32,833
Thanks!

431
00:16:32,856 --> 00:16:36,056
I live in the next room.

432
00:16:36,079 --> 00:16:38,649
Oh, nice to meet you!

433
00:16:38,673 --> 00:16:40,510
Likewise!

434
00:16:40,533 --> 00:16:42,700
Well, I'll be going now.

435
00:16:42,723 --> 00:16:44,141
Yes?

436
00:16:44,165 --> 00:16:45,665
Scene 15: Sharing the Joy of Sweets

437
00:16:45,665 --> 00:16:49,398
That looks delicious!

438
00:16:49,421 --> 00:16:52,488
It's so good!

439
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:54,845
What flavor is it?

440
00:16:54,868 --> 00:16:57,468
Strawberry.

441
00:16:57,491 --> 00:16:59,892
Lucky you.

442
00:16:59,915 --> 00:17:01,482
Want some?

443
00:17:01,505 --> 00:17:04,572
Can I have a bite?

444
00:17:04,595 --> 00:17:06,680
Sure.

445
00:17:06,703 --> 00:17:08,578
Thanks.

446
00:17:08,602 --> 00:17:10,968
Do you want a spoon?

447
00:17:10,991 --> 00:17:12,624
Yep.

448
00:17:12,647 --> 00:17:15,292
Here you go.

449
00:17:15,316 --> 00:17:17,805
Here I go!

450
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:19,036
How is it?

451
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:21,935
Sweet and delicious!

452
00:17:21,958 --> 00:17:23,958
Right?

453
00:17:23,981 --> 00:17:26,859
Where'd you buy it?

454
00:17:26,882 --> 00:17:30,060
The cake shop by the station.

455
00:17:30,083 --> 00:17:32,125
Is it a new place?

456
00:17:32,149 --> 00:17:34,206
Yeah, it is.

457
00:17:34,229 --> 00:17:36,596
I might check it out.

458
00:17:36,619 --> 00:17:39,452
I recommend it!

459
00:17:39,475 --> 00:17:41,761
Do they have chocolate too?

460
00:17:41,784 --> 00:17:44,551
I think so.

461
00:17:44,574 --> 00:17:47,223
I'll go buy some tomorrow.

462
00:17:47,247 --> 00:17:49,733
Shall we go together?

463
00:17:49,756 --> 00:17:51,125
Really?

464
00:17:51,149 --> 00:17:53,044
Yep.

465
00:17:53,067 --> 00:17:54,875
I'm so happy!

466
00:17:54,898 --> 00:17:57,732
I can't wait!

467
00:17:57,755 --> 00:17:59,255
Scene 16: Let's Go Home Together

468
00:17:59,255 --> 00:18:00,890
Are you leaving?

469
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:03,846
Yeah, I'm heading home.

470
00:18:03,869 --> 00:18:05,869
I'm leaving too.

471
00:18:05,892 --> 00:18:07,892
Let's go home together.

472
00:18:07,915 --> 00:18:10,548
Did you forget anything?

473
00:18:10,571 --> 00:18:12,338
I'm good.

474
00:18:12,361 --> 00:18:14,294
Alright, let's head out.

475
00:18:14,317 --> 00:18:17,559
Can I turn off the lights?

476
00:18:17,583 --> 00:18:20,416
Is anyone still here?

477
00:18:20,439 --> 00:18:22,439
I'm not sure.

478
00:18:22,462 --> 00:18:24,145
I'll go check.

479
00:18:24,169 --> 00:18:25,573
Thanks.

480
00:18:25,596 --> 00:18:27,535
No one's here.

481
00:18:27,558 --> 00:18:29,827
Okay, I'll turn them off.

482
00:18:29,851 --> 00:18:32,498
It's so dark.

483
00:18:32,521 --> 00:18:34,527
Should we lock up?

484
00:18:34,551 --> 00:18:37,017
The security guard will handle it.

485
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:38,528
Ah, got it.

486
00:18:38,552 --> 00:18:41,163
I'm hungry.

487
00:18:41,186 --> 00:18:42,802
Want some ramen?

488
00:18:42,825 --> 00:18:44,559
Nice.

489
00:18:44,582 --> 00:18:47,115
There's a new place.

490
00:18:47,138 --> 00:18:48,905
Near the station?

491
00:18:48,928 --> 00:18:50,261
Yeah.

492
00:18:50,284 --> 00:18:51,917
Let's check it out.

493
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:53,874
I heard it's delicious.

494
00:18:53,897 --> 00:18:55,630
Let's hurry.

495
00:18:55,653 --> 00:18:57,268
Let's go quick.

496
00:18:57,291 --> 00:18:58,791
Scene 17: Luggage and Japanese Study

497
00:18:58,791 --> 00:19:00,763
Excuse me.

498
00:19:00,787 --> 00:19:02,261
Yes?

499
00:19:02,284 --> 00:19:06,926
Could I leave my luggage here?

500
00:19:06,950 --> 00:19:08,983
Here you go.

501
00:19:09,006 --> 00:19:10,839
Thanks!

502
00:19:10,862 --> 00:19:13,337
That looks heavy.

503
00:19:13,361 --> 00:19:16,761
It's full of books.

504
00:19:16,784 --> 00:19:18,950
Are you a student?

505
00:19:18,973 --> 00:19:21,807
Yes, I am.

506
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:24,030
That must be tough.

507
00:19:24,052 --> 00:19:27,086
My exams are coming up.

508
00:19:27,109 --> 00:19:29,275
Good luck!

509
00:19:29,298 --> 00:19:31,132
Thanks!

510
00:19:31,156 --> 00:19:33,789
What are you studying?

511
00:19:33,812 --> 00:19:36,246
Japanese.

512
00:19:36,269 --> 00:19:39,669
Your Japanese is great!

513
00:19:39,692 --> 00:19:41,925
Not really.

514
00:19:41,948 --> 00:19:44,246
Are kanji difficult?

515
00:19:44,269 --> 00:19:47,436
They're really tough.

516
00:19:47,459 --> 00:19:49,392
Can you read them?

517
00:19:49,415 --> 00:19:52,111
Just a little.

518
00:19:52,134 --> 00:19:54,301
Wow, that's amazing!

519
00:19:54,324 --> 00:19:57,257
I'll work harder.

520
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:59,414
I'm rooting for you!

521
00:19:59,437 --> 00:20:01,703
That makes me happy!

522
00:20:01,726 --> 00:20:04,260
Please take it easy and rest.

523
00:20:04,283 --> 00:20:06,116
Yes?

524
00:20:06,139 --> 00:20:07,954
Take care.

525
00:20:07,977 --> 00:20:09,748
Thanks!

526
00:20:09,772 --> 00:20:11,972
Goodbye.

527
00:20:11,995 --> 00:20:13,495
Scene 18: Mastering Telephone Etiquette

528
00:20:13,495 --> 00:20:15,343
Hello?

529
00:20:15,366 --> 00:20:18,301
Oh, is this a good time?

530
00:20:18,324 --> 00:20:22,124
Sorry, I'm on the train right now.

531
00:20:22,147 --> 00:20:24,520
Oh, I see.

532
00:20:24,544 --> 00:20:27,547
Would it be okay if I call you back later?

533
00:20:27,571 --> 00:20:29,804
Of course.

534
00:20:29,827 --> 00:20:32,394
Was it something urgent?

535
00:20:32,417 --> 00:20:35,625
No, it's not urgent.

536
00:20:35,648 --> 00:20:37,656
That's a relief.

537
00:20:37,679 --> 00:20:40,688
When do you think you'll be done?

538
00:20:40,712 --> 00:20:43,562
I'll arrive in about 30 minutes.

539
00:20:43,585 --> 00:20:45,552
Understood.

540
00:20:45,575 --> 00:20:48,577
I'll call you once I get to the station.

541
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,453
I'll be waiting.

542
00:20:50,477 --> 00:20:53,843
It's about dinner plans, right?

543
00:20:53,866 --> 00:20:55,600
That's right.

544
00:20:55,623 --> 00:20:57,556
Have you decided on a place yet?

545
00:20:57,579 --> 00:21:00,583
I have three options in mind.

546
00:21:00,607 --> 00:21:03,503
Let's decide together later.

547
00:21:03,526 --> 00:21:04,893
Yes?

548
00:21:04,916 --> 00:21:07,516
I'm starving.

549
00:21:07,539 --> 00:21:10,017
Me too.

550
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:12,460
Alright, talk to you later.

551
00:21:12,483 --> 00:21:14,292
Take care.

552
00:21:14,316 --> 00:21:16,282
Thanks.

553
00:21:16,305 --> 00:21:18,381
I'll hang up now.

554
00:21:18,404 --> 00:21:19,884
Yep.

555
00:21:19,908 --> 00:21:21,755
Excuse me.

556
00:21:21,779 --> 00:21:23,183
Yes?

557
00:21:23,206 --> 00:21:25,206
See you later.

558
00:21:25,229 --> 00:21:26,729
Scene 19: Planning Your Dream Trip

559
00:21:26,729 --> 00:21:28,999
Excuse me.

560
00:21:29,023 --> 00:21:31,508
Welcome! How can I help you today?

561
00:21:31,531 --> 00:21:35,998
May I take this brochure with me?

562
00:21:36,021 --> 00:21:39,289
Here you go.

563
00:21:39,312 --> 00:21:41,146
Thanks!

564
00:21:41,170 --> 00:21:44,036
Are you considering a trip?

565
00:21:44,059 --> 00:21:47,393
Yes, for the winter break.

566
00:21:47,416 --> 00:21:50,082
Where are you thinking of going?

567
00:21:50,105 --> 00:21:53,272
I'd love to visit Hokkaido.

568
00:21:53,295 --> 00:21:55,163
For skiing?

569
00:21:55,187 --> 00:21:58,438
No, for the hot springs.

570
00:21:58,462 --> 00:22:01,262
Hot springs sound wonderful.

571
00:22:01,285 --> 00:22:04,618
I'd also love to try some delicious food.

572
00:22:04,641 --> 00:22:07,879
I recommend trying crab—it's amazing there!

573
00:22:07,903 --> 00:22:09,436
Nice!

574
00:22:09,459 --> 00:22:12,197
We also have tour packages available.

575
00:22:12,220 --> 00:22:14,713
Are the tours a good deal?

576
00:22:14,737 --> 00:22:17,672
Yes, they're very cost-effective.

577
00:22:17,695 --> 00:22:20,309
Does it include flights as well?

578
00:22:20,333 --> 00:22:23,799
Yes, and it includes hotel accommodations too.

579
00:22:23,822 --> 00:22:25,822
That's so convenient!

580
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:29,021
Would you like me to prepare a quote for you?

581
00:22:29,045 --> 00:22:31,845
I don't have time today.

582
00:22:31,868 --> 00:22:33,959
Got it.

583
00:22:33,982 --> 00:22:37,401
I'll read the brochure at home.

584
00:22:37,425 --> 00:22:40,440
We look forward to seeing you again.

585
00:22:40,463 --> 00:22:42,796
I'll come back this weekend.

586
00:22:42,819 --> 00:22:45,429
Thanks!

587
00:22:45,453 --> 00:22:47,294
Excuse me.

588
00:22:47,318 --> 00:22:49,998
Thank you so much.

589
00:22:50,021 --> 00:22:51,521
Scene 20: How to Ask for Permission Politely

590
00:22:51,521 --> 00:22:52,955
Teacher.

591
00:22:52,978 --> 00:22:54,597
Yes?

592
00:22:54,620 --> 00:22:57,987
May I ask you something?

593
00:22:58,010 --> 00:22:59,946
Sure, what is it?

594
00:22:59,970 --> 00:23:03,218
I don’t understand this grammar point.

595
00:23:03,241 --> 00:23:05,175
Where are the fitting rooms?

596
00:23:05,198 --> 00:23:07,472
Right here.

597
00:23:07,495 --> 00:23:10,062
Ah, this one.

598
00:23:10,085 --> 00:23:11,718
Yes?

599
00:23:11,741 --> 00:23:15,120
This is an expression for permission.

600
00:23:15,144 --> 00:23:17,110
Permission?

601
00:23:17,133 --> 00:23:18,808
Yes?

602
00:23:18,832 --> 00:23:21,399
It’s used when asking for something.

603
00:23:21,422 --> 00:23:24,116
Could you give me an example?

604
00:23:24,139 --> 00:23:27,312
Like, 'May I open the window?'

605
00:23:27,335 --> 00:23:28,770
That kind of thing.

606
00:23:28,794 --> 00:23:30,605
I see.

607
00:23:30,628 --> 00:23:33,407
Do you understand now?

608
00:23:33,430 --> 00:23:35,797
Yes, I get it.

609
00:23:35,820 --> 00:23:38,420
Any other questions?

610
00:23:38,443 --> 00:23:41,276
No, I’m good.

611
00:23:41,299 --> 00:23:43,869
Have you finished your homework?

612
00:23:43,893 --> 00:23:46,493
I’ve done half of it.

613
00:23:46,516 --> 00:23:48,563
Is it difficult?

614
00:23:48,587 --> 00:23:51,620
The kanji are tough.

615
00:23:51,643 --> 00:23:54,701
Practice every day, okay?

616
00:23:54,724 --> 00:23:57,094
Yes, I’ll do my best!

617
00:23:57,117 --> 00:24:00,117
Ask me if you don’t understand something.

618
00:24:00,140 --> 00:24:01,941
Thanks!

619
00:24:01,964 --> 00:24:04,842
See you tomorrow!

620
00:24:04,866 --> 00:24:06,633
Goodbye.

621
00:24:06,656 --> 00:24:08,623
Goodbye.

622
00:24:18,282 --> 00:24:19,782
Scene 1: Basic Japanese Greetings and Seat Confirmation

623
00:24:19,782 --> 00:24:22,180
Listening Test

624
00:24:22,180 --> 00:24:24,913
Excuse me.

625
00:24:28,733 --> 00:24:30,313
Yes?

626
00:24:30,336 --> 00:24:33,242
Listening Test

627
00:24:33,242 --> 00:24:36,624
Is this seat taken?

628
00:24:36,624 --> 00:24:41,295
N + が + 空(あ)く = N is available
空(あ)く = to be empty / to be available

629
00:24:41,319 --> 00:24:43,585
Listening Test

630
00:24:43,585 --> 00:24:46,138
Oh, no, it's free.

631
00:24:49,728 --> 00:24:52,724
Listening Test

632
00:24:52,724 --> 00:24:56,195
Mind if I sit here?

633
00:24:56,195 --> 00:25:00,991
Vて + も + 大丈夫(だいじょうぶ) + ですか = May I V?
大丈夫(だいじょうぶ) (all right) ↔ 大変(たいへん) (tough)

634
00:25:01,014 --> 00:25:02,881
Go ahead.

635
00:25:02,904 --> 00:25:05,237
Listening Test

636
00:25:05,237 --> 00:25:07,876
Thanks!

637
00:25:11,577 --> 00:25:13,843
No problem.

638
00:25:13,866 --> 00:25:16,533
Listening Test

639
00:25:16,533 --> 00:25:19,599
You have a lot of luggage.

640
00:25:19,599 --> 00:25:23,833
いA + です + ね = A, isn’t it?
荷物(にもつ) = luggage
多(おお)い (many) ↔ 少(すく)ない (few)

641
00:25:23,856 --> 00:25:26,134
Listening Test

642
00:25:26,134 --> 00:25:28,711
Excuse me.

643
00:25:32,367 --> 00:25:34,834
Listening Test

644
00:25:34,834 --> 00:25:37,626
It's fine, really.

645
00:25:41,549 --> 00:25:44,649
Listening Test

646
00:25:44,649 --> 00:25:48,230
I'll just move it a bit.

647
00:25:48,230 --> 00:25:53,165
Vます + ね = I will V
少(すこ)し (a little) ↔ たくさん (a lot)
どかす = to move aside

648
00:25:53,188 --> 00:25:55,221
Listening Test

649
00:25:55,221 --> 00:25:57,488
Excuse me.

650
00:26:00,678 --> 00:26:02,868
Listening Test

651
00:26:02,868 --> 00:26:05,368
Don't worry about it.

652
00:26:08,857 --> 00:26:10,847
Listening Test

653
00:26:10,847 --> 00:26:13,081
Going on a trip?

654
00:26:13,081 --> 00:26:16,214
N + ですか = Is it N?
旅行(りょこう) = travel / trip

655
00:26:16,237 --> 00:26:18,137
Yes?

656
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:20,754
Listening Test

657
00:26:20,754 --> 00:26:23,727
Where to?

658
00:26:23,727 --> 00:26:27,864
N (place) + に + 行(い)く = go to N
どこ = where

659
00:26:27,887 --> 00:26:30,354
Listening Test

660
00:26:30,354 --> 00:26:33,139
Tokyo.

661
00:26:33,139 --> 00:26:37,039
N (place) + に + 行(い)く = go to N
東京(とうきょう) = Tokyo

662
00:26:37,062 --> 00:26:39,180
Listening Test

663
00:26:39,180 --> 00:26:41,561
Nice!

664
00:26:41,561 --> 00:26:44,894
いA + です + ね = That sounds A

665
00:26:44,917 --> 00:26:46,903
Yes?

666
00:26:46,926 --> 00:26:49,116
Listening Test

667
00:26:49,116 --> 00:26:51,583
For sightseeing?

668
00:26:51,583 --> 00:26:55,050
N + ですか = Is it N?
観光(かんこう) = sightseeing

669
00:26:55,073 --> 00:26:57,211
Listening Test

670
00:26:57,211 --> 00:26:59,644
That's right.

671
00:27:03,045 --> 00:27:06,045
Listening Test

672
00:27:06,045 --> 00:27:09,545
I'm here for work.

673
00:27:09,545 --> 00:27:14,378
N (person) + は + N + です = N is N
私(わたし) = I / me
仕事(しごと) = work / job

674
00:27:14,401 --> 00:27:16,735
Listening Test

675
00:27:16,735 --> 00:27:19,401
Hope it goes well for you.

676
00:27:19,401 --> 00:27:23,101
お疲(つか)れ様(さま) = Thank you for your hard work

677
00:27:23,124 --> 00:27:25,358
Listening Test

678
00:27:25,358 --> 00:27:27,858
Thanks!

679
00:27:31,359 --> 00:27:34,193
Listening Test

680
00:27:34,193 --> 00:27:37,459
How many days are you staying?

681
00:27:37,459 --> 00:27:41,967
何日(なんにち) = how many days
何日(なんにち) = how many days / which day of the month

682
00:27:41,991 --> 00:27:44,257
Listening Test

683
00:27:44,257 --> 00:27:46,791
Three days.

684
00:27:46,791 --> 00:27:50,335
三日(みっか) = three days

685
00:27:50,358 --> 00:27:52,670
Listening Test

686
00:27:52,670 --> 00:27:55,303
That's a long trip.

687
00:27:55,303 --> 00:27:58,970
いA + です + ね = A, isn’t it?
長(なが)い (long) ↔ 短(みじか)い (short)

688
00:27:58,993 --> 00:28:00,893
Go ahead.

689
00:28:00,916 --> 00:28:03,816
Listening Test

690
00:28:03,816 --> 00:28:07,175
Take care, okay?

691
00:28:07,175 --> 00:28:11,808
気(き)をつける = Take care
気(き)をつける = to be careful / to take care

692
00:28:11,831 --> 00:28:13,331
Scene 2: Greetings and Cherry Blossom Photography

693
00:28:13,331 --> 00:28:15,898
Listening Test

694
00:28:15,898 --> 00:28:18,837
Excuse me.

695
00:28:22,932 --> 00:28:24,912
Yes?

696
00:28:24,935 --> 00:28:28,235
Listening Test

697
00:28:28,235 --> 00:28:32,102
Is it okay if I take a photo?

698
00:28:32,102 --> 00:28:37,402
N + 大丈夫(だいじょうぶ)ですか = Is N okay?
写真(しゃしん) = photo
大丈夫(だいじょうぶ) (all right) ↔ 大変(たいへん) (tough)

699
00:28:37,425 --> 00:28:39,983
Listening Test

700
00:28:39,983 --> 00:28:42,932
Here?

701
00:28:42,932 --> 00:28:47,000
N + ですか = Is it N?

702
00:28:47,024 --> 00:28:49,290
Yes?

703
00:28:49,313 --> 00:28:51,847
Listening Test

704
00:28:51,847 --> 00:28:54,747
Sure, go ahead.

705
00:28:54,747 --> 00:28:58,780
いA + ですよ = It is A (informing/confirming)

706
00:28:58,803 --> 00:29:01,470
Listening Test

707
00:29:01,470 --> 00:29:04,536
Thanks!

708
00:29:08,793 --> 00:29:11,859
Listening Test

709
00:29:11,859 --> 00:29:15,398
What are you taking a picture of?

710
00:29:15,398 --> 00:29:20,275
N + を + Vますか = Do you V N?
撮(と)ります = take (a photo)

711
00:29:20,299 --> 00:29:23,232
Listening Test

712
00:29:23,232 --> 00:29:26,629
Those flowers over there.

713
00:29:26,629 --> 00:29:31,304
こ/そ/あ/ど + N = this / that / which N
花(はな) = flower

714
00:29:31,327 --> 00:29:33,994
Listening Test

715
00:29:33,994 --> 00:29:37,060
They're beautiful.

716
00:29:37,060 --> 00:29:41,294
なA + ですね = It is A, isn’t it?
綺麗(きれい) (beautiful) ↔ 汚(きたな)い (dirty)

717
00:29:41,317 --> 00:29:43,756
Go ahead.

718
00:29:43,779 --> 00:29:46,446
Listening Test

719
00:29:46,446 --> 00:29:49,523
Are those cherry blossoms?

720
00:29:49,523 --> 00:29:53,789
N + ですか = Is it N?
桜(さくら) = cherry blossom

721
00:29:53,812 --> 00:29:56,392
Listening Test

722
00:29:56,392 --> 00:29:59,342
That's right.

723
00:30:03,465 --> 00:30:06,432
Listening Test

724
00:30:06,432 --> 00:30:09,865
They're already blooming.

725
00:30:09,865 --> 00:30:14,603
Vています = is/are V-ing
咲(さ)きます = bloom

726
00:30:14,627 --> 00:30:17,860
Listening Test

727
00:30:17,860 --> 00:30:21,628
It's warm, so they are.

728
00:30:21,628 --> 00:30:26,804
いA + から = because A
暖(あたた)かい (warm) ↔ 涼(すず)しい (cool)

729
00:30:26,828 --> 00:30:29,362
Listening Test

730
00:30:29,362 --> 00:30:32,262
Yeah, it is.

731
00:30:36,318 --> 00:30:39,451
Listening Test

732
00:30:39,451 --> 00:30:43,085
I come here every year.

733
00:30:43,085 --> 00:30:48,118
N (time) + に + N (place) + Vます = V to/at N
Example: 毎年 (every year)

734
00:30:48,141 --> 00:30:50,908
Listening Test

735
00:30:50,908 --> 00:30:54,097
Really?

736
00:30:54,097 --> 00:30:58,530
な-adjective + ですか = Is it [adjective]?
Example: 本当 (truth / reality)

737
00:30:58,553 --> 00:31:00,686
Yes?

738
00:31:00,709 --> 00:31:03,876
Listening Test

739
00:31:03,876 --> 00:31:07,576
This is my first time.

740
00:31:07,576 --> 00:31:12,676
N1 + は + N2 + です = N1 is N2
Example: 初めて (first time)

741
00:31:12,699 --> 00:31:15,773
Listening Test

742
00:31:15,773 --> 00:31:19,348
It's a great spot.

743
00:31:19,348 --> 00:31:24,281
な-adjective + N = [adjective] N
Example: 場所 (place)

744
00:31:24,304 --> 00:31:27,338
Listening Test

745
00:31:27,338 --> 00:31:30,841
Can I see the photo?

746
00:31:30,841 --> 00:31:35,676
Vてください = Please do [verb]
Example: 見せます (show)

747
00:31:35,699 --> 00:31:38,475
Listening Test

748
00:31:38,475 --> 00:31:41,675
Sure, go ahead.

749
00:31:41,675 --> 00:31:46,142
い-adjective + ですよ = It is [adjective] (informing)

750
00:31:46,165 --> 00:31:48,998
Listening Test

751
00:31:48,998 --> 00:31:52,233
Wow, that's amazing!

752
00:31:52,233 --> 00:31:56,733
い-adjective + ですね = It is [adjective], isn’t it?

753
00:31:56,756 --> 00:31:59,889
Listening Test

754
00:31:59,889 --> 00:32:03,556
It's a good camera.

755
00:32:03,556 --> 00:32:08,589
い-adjective + んです = It is that [adjective] (explanation)

756
00:32:08,612 --> 00:32:11,479
Listening Test

757
00:32:11,479 --> 00:32:14,787
You take photos like a pro!

758
00:32:14,787 --> 00:32:19,354
N + みたいです = Looks like N / Is like N

759
00:32:19,377 --> 00:32:22,349
Listening Test

760
00:32:22,349 --> 00:32:25,815
Oh, not at all.

761
00:32:25,815 --> 00:32:30,583
とんでもない = Not at all! / Don’t mention it!

762
00:32:30,606 --> 00:32:34,398
Listening Test

763
00:32:34,398 --> 00:32:38,870
I want a camera too.

764
00:32:38,870 --> 00:32:44,987
N + が + 欲しいです = I want N
Example: 欲しい (want)

765
00:32:45,011 --> 00:32:47,644
Listening Test

766
00:32:47,644 --> 00:32:50,678
It's a lot of fun.

767
00:32:50,678 --> 00:32:54,844
い-adjective + ですよ = It is [adjective] (informing)
Example: 楽しい (fun) ↔ つまらない (boring)

768
00:32:54,867 --> 00:32:57,737
Listening Test

769
00:32:57,737 --> 00:33:01,071
I'll look into it.

770
00:33:01,071 --> 00:33:05,704
Vてみます = Try doing [verb]
Example: 探します (look for / search)

771
00:33:05,727 --> 00:33:07,227
Scene 3: Borrowing a Pen

772
00:33:07,227 --> 00:33:09,294
Hey.

773
00:33:09,317 --> 00:33:10,984
Yeah?

774
00:33:11,007 --> 00:33:14,584
Listening Test

775
00:33:14,584 --> 00:33:18,782
Can I borrow a pen for a sec?

776
00:33:18,782 --> 00:33:24,549
Vても + いいかな = I wonder if it’s okay to [verb]
Example: 借りる (borrow)

777
00:33:24,572 --> 00:33:26,438
Sure.

778
00:33:26,461 --> 00:33:28,395
Listening Test

779
00:33:28,395 --> 00:33:30,530
Thanks.

780
00:33:33,586 --> 00:33:36,419
Listening Test

781
00:33:36,419 --> 00:33:39,686
I’ve got red and black.

782
00:33:39,686 --> 00:33:44,186
N1 と N2 が ある = There is N1 and N2
Example: 赤 (red) ↔ 黒 (black)

783
00:33:44,209 --> 00:33:46,485
Listening Test

784
00:33:46,485 --> 00:33:49,080
Black, please.

785
00:33:49,080 --> 00:33:52,677
N を お 願い = [Noun], please

786
00:33:52,701 --> 00:33:54,617
Yes?

787
00:33:54,640 --> 00:33:56,940
Listening Test

788
00:33:56,940 --> 00:33:59,522
You’re a lifesaver.

789
00:33:59,522 --> 00:34:03,155
助かった = That was a huge help!
Example: 助かる (to be saved / helped)

790
00:34:03,178 --> 00:34:05,478
Listening Test

791
00:34:05,478 --> 00:34:08,071
What are you writing?

792
00:34:08,071 --> 00:34:11,738
N を Vの = [Verb] the N?
Example: 書く (write)

793
00:34:11,761 --> 00:34:14,094
Listening Test

794
00:34:14,094 --> 00:34:16,730
Just a note.

795
00:34:16,730 --> 00:34:20,401
N だよ = It’s [noun]
Example: メモ (memo / note)

796
00:34:20,424 --> 00:34:22,500
Listening Test

797
00:34:22,500 --> 00:34:24,819
Ah, got it.

798
00:34:24,819 --> 00:34:28,098
そうなんだ = I see / Oh, really?

799
00:34:28,122 --> 00:34:30,989
Listening Test

800
00:34:30,989 --> 00:34:34,289
I’m jotting down a phone number.

801
00:34:34,289 --> 00:34:38,827
Vんだ = [Verb] (explanation / emphasis)
Example: 電話番号 (phone number)

802
00:34:38,850 --> 00:34:41,550
Listening Test

803
00:34:41,550 --> 00:34:44,650
Whose number?

804
00:34:44,650 --> 00:34:48,950
誰 の N = Whose N?
Example: 誰 (who)

805
00:34:48,973 --> 00:34:51,363
Listening Test

806
00:34:51,363 --> 00:34:54,076
A friend’s.

807
00:34:54,076 --> 00:34:57,860
N だよ = It’s [noun]
Example: 友達 (friend)

808
00:34:57,884 --> 00:34:59,880
Meeting up?

809
00:34:59,903 --> 00:35:01,605
Yep.

810
00:35:01,629 --> 00:35:03,862
Listening Test

811
00:35:03,862 --> 00:35:06,364
When?

812
00:35:06,364 --> 00:35:09,864
いつ Vの = When do you [verb]?
Example: いつ (when)

813
00:35:09,887 --> 00:35:12,154
Listening Test

814
00:35:12,154 --> 00:35:14,687
Tomorrow.

815
00:35:14,687 --> 00:35:18,220
N だよ = It’s [noun]
Example: 明日 (tomorrow)

816
00:35:18,243 --> 00:35:20,077
Where?

817
00:35:20,100 --> 00:35:22,768
Listening Test

818
00:35:22,768 --> 00:35:25,843
In front of the station.

819
00:35:25,843 --> 00:35:30,109
N の 前 = In front of N
Example: 駅 (station)
前 (front) ↔ 後ろ (back)

820
00:35:30,132 --> 00:35:32,118
Nice.

821
00:35:32,142 --> 00:35:34,708
Listening Test

822
00:35:34,708 --> 00:35:37,646
We’re watching a movie.

823
00:35:37,646 --> 00:35:41,746
N を Vんだ = [Verb] the N (explanation / emphasis)
Example: 映画 (movie) / 見る (watch)

824
00:35:41,769 --> 00:35:43,888
Listening Test

825
00:35:43,888 --> 00:35:46,269
What kind?

826
00:35:46,269 --> 00:35:49,627
何 の N = What kind of N?

827
00:35:49,651 --> 00:35:52,284
Listening Test

828
00:35:52,284 --> 00:35:55,317
An anime.

829
00:35:55,317 --> 00:35:59,502
N だよ = It’s [noun]
Example: アニメ (anime / animation)

830
00:35:59,526 --> 00:36:02,160
Listening Test

831
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:05,193
Sounds fun.

832
00:36:05,193 --> 00:36:09,360
い-adjective + そう = Looks / sounds [adjective]
Example: 面白い (interesting) ↔ つまらない (boring)

833
00:36:09,383 --> 00:36:12,283
Listening Test

834
00:36:12,283 --> 00:36:15,616
I’ve been wanting to see it for ages.

835
00:36:15,616 --> 00:36:20,214
Vたかった = Wanted to [verb]
Example: ずっと (all the time / for a long time)

836
00:36:20,237 --> 00:36:22,671
Listening Test

837
00:36:22,671 --> 00:36:25,420
Have a great time!

838
00:36:25,420 --> 00:36:29,253
Vて + くる = Go and [verb]
Example: 楽しむ (enjoy)

839
00:36:29,276 --> 00:36:31,576
Listening Test

840
00:36:31,576 --> 00:36:34,169
Here’s your pen back.

841
00:36:34,169 --> 00:36:37,803
Vね = [Verb], right? (sentence-ending particle)
Example: 返す (return)

842
00:36:37,827 --> 00:36:39,960
Thanks.

843
00:36:39,983 --> 00:36:41,483
Scene 4: Toothache and Leaving Work Early

844
00:36:41,483 --> 00:36:43,597
Listening Test

845
00:36:43,597 --> 00:36:45,966
Manager.

846
00:36:49,339 --> 00:36:51,291
Listening Test

847
00:36:51,291 --> 00:36:53,464
Yes?

848
00:36:56,554 --> 00:36:59,054
Listening Test

849
00:36:59,054 --> 00:37:01,887
Hope it goes well for you.

850
00:37:05,859 --> 00:37:08,438
Listening Test

851
00:37:08,438 --> 00:37:11,393
Good work today.

852
00:37:15,526 --> 00:37:20,496
Listening Test

853
00:37:20,496 --> 00:37:26,446
Could I leave a little early today?

854
00:37:26,446 --> 00:37:34,546
Vさせて + もらえませんか = Could you please let me [verb]?
Example: 上がる (leave work / finish work)

855
00:37:34,569 --> 00:37:37,302
Listening Test

856
00:37:37,302 --> 00:37:40,436
What’s up?

857
00:37:40,436 --> 00:37:44,782
どうした = What happened? / What’s wrong?

858
00:37:44,805 --> 00:37:47,505
Listening Test

859
00:37:47,505 --> 00:37:50,607
I need to go to the hospital.

860
00:37:50,607 --> 00:37:54,941
Vたい + んです = I want to [verb]...
Example: 病院 (hospital)

861
00:37:54,964 --> 00:37:58,540
Listening Test

862
00:37:58,540 --> 00:38:02,773
Are you feeling unwell?

863
00:38:02,773 --> 00:38:08,540
い-adjective + い + んです = Is it [adjective]?
Example: 体調 (physical condition)

864
00:38:08,563 --> 00:38:11,829
Listening Test

865
00:38:11,829 --> 00:38:15,623
No, it’s the dentist.

866
00:38:15,623 --> 00:38:20,857
N + です = It is [noun].
Example: 歯医者 (dentist)

867
00:38:20,880 --> 00:38:24,186
Listening Test

868
00:38:24,186 --> 00:38:28,052
Toothache?

869
00:38:28,052 --> 00:38:33,386
い-adjective + い + んです = Does it hurt?
Example: 痛い (painful / hurt)

870
00:38:33,409 --> 00:38:35,242
Yes?

871
00:38:35,265 --> 00:38:38,935
Listening Test

872
00:38:38,935 --> 00:38:43,268
That’s rough.

873
00:38:43,268 --> 00:38:49,201
な-adjective + ですね = That sounds [adjective]...
Example: 大変 (tough / hard)

874
00:38:49,224 --> 00:38:51,174
Listening Test

875
00:38:51,174 --> 00:38:53,347
Excuse me.

876
00:38:56,437 --> 00:38:59,907
Listening Test

877
00:38:59,907 --> 00:39:03,985
What time are you leaving?

878
00:39:03,985 --> 00:39:09,618
何時 に + Vますか = What time do you [verb]?

879
00:39:09,641 --> 00:39:12,108
Listening Test

880
00:39:12,108 --> 00:39:14,892
Would 3 PM work?

881
00:39:14,892 --> 00:39:18,759
N + でも + いいですか = Is [noun] okay?

882
00:39:18,782 --> 00:39:21,650
Listening Test

883
00:39:21,650 --> 00:39:24,983
Sure, go ahead.

884
00:39:29,593 --> 00:39:32,032
Listening Test

885
00:39:32,032 --> 00:39:34,813
Thanks!

886
00:39:38,702 --> 00:39:42,140
Listening Test

887
00:39:42,140 --> 00:39:46,174
Finished your work?

888
00:39:46,174 --> 00:39:51,707
仕事 = work
終わる = to finish

889
00:39:51,730 --> 00:39:53,682
Listening Test

890
00:39:53,682 --> 00:39:55,849
Yes?

891
00:39:58,938 --> 00:40:02,213
Listening Test

892
00:40:02,213 --> 00:40:06,047
Did you complete the documents?

893
00:40:06,047 --> 00:40:11,313
資料 = document / material
できる = to be ready / completed

894
00:40:11,336 --> 00:40:14,309
Listening Test

895
00:40:14,309 --> 00:40:17,776
They’re on my desk.

896
00:40:17,776 --> 00:40:22,563
机 = desk

897
00:40:22,587 --> 00:40:25,142
Listening Test

898
00:40:25,142 --> 00:40:28,079
Understood.

899
00:40:32,168 --> 00:40:35,402
Listening Test

900
00:40:35,402 --> 00:40:39,141
I’ll be in as usual tomorrow.

901
00:40:39,141 --> 00:40:44,300
明日 = tomorrow

902
00:40:44,324 --> 00:40:46,903
Listening Test

903
00:40:46,903 --> 00:40:49,852
Take it easy.

904
00:40:49,852 --> 00:40:53,952
無理しないで = Don’t overdo it / Take it easy

905
00:40:53,975 --> 00:40:56,925
Listening Test

906
00:40:56,925 --> 00:41:00,358
Thanks!

907
00:41:05,122 --> 00:41:07,422
Listening Test

908
00:41:07,422 --> 00:41:10,056
Take care.

909
00:41:10,056 --> 00:41:13,722
お大事に = Take care / Get well soon

910
00:41:13,745 --> 00:41:16,379
Listening Test

911
00:41:16,379 --> 00:41:19,362
Excuse me.

912
00:41:23,531 --> 00:41:25,964
Listening Test

913
00:41:25,964 --> 00:41:28,708
Good work today.

914
00:41:32,564 --> 00:41:34,064
Scene 5: Adjusting the Temperature in Conversation

915
00:41:34,064 --> 00:41:36,256
Hey.

916
00:41:36,280 --> 00:41:38,113
Yep.

917
00:41:38,136 --> 00:41:41,708
Listening Test

918
00:41:41,708 --> 00:41:45,900
Can I turn down the AC a bit?

919
00:41:45,900 --> 00:41:51,653
い-adjective + く + する / な-adjective + に + する = Make it [adjective]
Example: 弱い (weak) ↔ 強い (strong)

920
00:41:51,676 --> 00:41:54,143
Are you cold?

921
00:41:54,166 --> 00:41:57,466
Listening Test

922
00:41:57,466 --> 00:42:01,299
A little, yeah.

923
00:42:01,299 --> 00:42:06,576
かな = I wonder if...
Example: 少し (a little) ↔ たくさん (a lot)

924
00:42:06,600 --> 00:42:08,700
Sure.

925
00:42:08,723 --> 00:42:10,789
Listening Test

926
00:42:10,789 --> 00:42:13,089
Thanks.

927
00:42:16,346 --> 00:42:19,530
Listening Test

928
00:42:19,530 --> 00:42:23,264
The remote’s right there.

929
00:42:23,264 --> 00:42:28,373
N + に + ある = There is N (e.g., 'remote control')

930
00:42:28,396 --> 00:42:30,696
Listening Test

931
00:42:30,696 --> 00:42:33,289
Got it.

932
00:42:33,289 --> 00:42:36,922
Vた = Got it! / Understood!

933
00:42:36,945 --> 00:42:39,245
Listening Test

934
00:42:39,245 --> 00:42:41,878
What temperature should I set it to?

935
00:42:41,878 --> 00:42:45,545
何度(なんど) + に + する = Set to what temperature? (e.g., 'What temperature?' / 'How many degrees?')

936
00:42:45,568 --> 00:42:48,760
Listening Test

937
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:52,493
Twenty-six degrees is fine.

938
00:42:52,493 --> 00:42:57,611
N + で + いい = N is fine (e.g., '26 degrees is fine')

939
00:42:57,635 --> 00:42:59,631
Sure.

940
00:42:59,654 --> 00:43:02,800
Listening Test

941
00:43:02,800 --> 00:43:06,467
I’ll lower the fan speed too.

942
00:43:06,467 --> 00:43:11,534
N + も = N also (e.g., 'wind' / 'airflow')

943
00:43:11,557 --> 00:43:13,555
Listening Test

944
00:43:13,555 --> 00:43:15,788
Got it.

945
00:43:18,944 --> 00:43:21,244
Listening Test

946
00:43:21,244 --> 00:43:23,838
Sorry about that.

947
00:43:27,495 --> 00:43:30,428
Listening Test

948
00:43:30,428 --> 00:43:33,812
It’s totally fine.

949
00:43:33,812 --> 00:43:38,483
全然(ぜんぜん) + なA = Completely... / Totally... (e.g., 'not at all' / 'totally')

950
00:43:38,507 --> 00:43:41,217
Listening Test

951
00:43:41,217 --> 00:43:44,350
It’s hot outside, huh?

952
00:43:44,350 --> 00:43:48,683
N + は + いA + ね = N is..., isn’t it? (e.g., 'outside' vs. 'inside')

953
00:43:48,706 --> 00:43:51,673
Listening Test

954
00:43:51,673 --> 00:43:55,112
So hot.

955
00:43:55,112 --> 00:43:59,857
すごく + いA = Very... (e.g., 'hot' vs. 'cold')

956
00:43:59,881 --> 00:44:02,947
Listening Test

957
00:44:02,947 --> 00:44:06,494
It’s summer, after all.

958
00:44:06,494 --> 00:44:11,394
N + だから = Because it’s N (e.g., 'summer' vs. 'winter')

959
00:44:11,417 --> 00:44:13,161
Yep.

960
00:44:13,185 --> 00:44:15,685
Listening Test

961
00:44:15,685 --> 00:44:18,551
Want some ice cream?

962
00:44:18,551 --> 00:44:22,506
V + ？ = Do you...? / Will you...? (e.g., 'ice cream')

963
00:44:22,529 --> 00:44:24,796
Yeah, I’ll have some.

964
00:44:24,819 --> 00:44:27,575
Listening Test

965
00:44:27,575 --> 00:44:30,768
It’s in the fridge.

966
00:44:30,768 --> 00:44:35,157
N + に + ある = There is N (e.g., 'refrigerator')

967
00:44:35,181 --> 00:44:37,283
Listening Test

968
00:44:37,283 --> 00:44:39,641
I’ll grab it.

969
00:44:39,641 --> 00:44:42,944
Vて + くる = Go and... (e.g., 'get' / 'take')

970
00:44:42,967 --> 00:44:44,951
Thanks.

971
00:44:44,975 --> 00:44:47,167
Listening Test

972
00:44:47,167 --> 00:44:49,643
Is chocolate okay?

973
00:44:49,643 --> 00:44:53,111
N + で + いい = N is fine (e.g., 'chocolate is fine')

974
00:44:53,134 --> 00:44:55,290
Yep.

975
00:44:55,313 --> 00:44:57,653
Listening Test

976
00:44:57,653 --> 00:45:00,320
Here you go.

977
00:45:04,049 --> 00:45:06,017
Listening Test

978
00:45:06,017 --> 00:45:08,211
Thanks.

979
00:45:11,335 --> 00:45:14,168
Listening Test

980
00:45:14,168 --> 00:45:17,403
This is good.

981
00:45:17,403 --> 00:45:21,870
いA + ね = It’s..., isn’t it? (e.g., 'delicious' vs. 'bad tasting')

982
00:45:21,894 --> 00:45:23,394
Scene 6: Trying on Clothes Conversation

983
00:45:23,394 --> 00:45:25,782
Listening Test

984
00:45:25,782 --> 00:45:28,499
Excuse me.

985
00:45:32,310 --> 00:45:34,043
Yes?

986
00:45:34,066 --> 00:45:37,899
Listening Test

987
00:45:37,899 --> 00:45:42,405
Can I try this on?

988
00:45:42,405 --> 00:45:48,572
Vて + もいいですか = May I...? (e.g., 'try on clothes')

989
00:45:48,595 --> 00:45:51,147
Listening Test

990
00:45:51,147 --> 00:45:54,080
Of course.

991
00:45:54,080 --> 00:45:58,147
勿論(もちろん) = Of course!

992
00:45:58,170 --> 00:46:00,404
Listening Test

993
00:46:00,404 --> 00:46:02,937
Where are the fitting rooms?

994
00:46:02,937 --> 00:46:06,450
どこ + ですか = Where is...? (e.g., 'where')

995
00:46:06,474 --> 00:46:09,307
Listening Test

996
00:46:09,307 --> 00:46:12,574
Right over there.

997
00:46:12,574 --> 00:46:17,074
あちら = Over there

998
00:46:17,097 --> 00:46:19,563
Listening Test

999
00:46:19,563 --> 00:46:22,344
Thanks!

1000
00:46:26,235 --> 00:46:29,424
Listening Test

1001
00:46:29,424 --> 00:46:33,158
How’s the size?

1002
00:46:33,158 --> 00:46:38,296
N + は + どうですか = How is N? (e.g., 'size')

1003
00:46:38,319 --> 00:46:41,752
Listening Test

1004
00:46:41,752 --> 00:46:45,786
It’s a little big.

1005
00:46:45,786 --> 00:46:51,295
いA（〜い） + です = It is... (e.g., 'big' vs. 'small')

1006
00:46:51,318 --> 00:46:54,551
Listening Test

1007
00:46:54,551 --> 00:46:58,304
I’ll bring you a smaller size.

1008
00:46:58,304 --> 00:47:03,485
お + V（stem） + します = I will (humbly)... (e.g., 'hold' / 'carry')

1009
00:47:03,508 --> 00:47:06,014
Listening Test

1010
00:47:06,014 --> 00:47:08,881
Please do.

1011
00:47:12,887 --> 00:47:15,320
Listening Test

1012
00:47:15,320 --> 00:47:18,087
Here you go.

1013
00:47:18,087 --> 00:47:21,925
待(ま)つ = To wait

1014
00:47:21,949 --> 00:47:24,219
Listening Test

1015
00:47:24,219 --> 00:47:26,786
Thanks!

1016
00:47:30,387 --> 00:47:32,687
Listening Test

1017
00:47:32,687 --> 00:47:35,282
How does it fit?

1018
00:47:35,282 --> 00:47:38,915
いかが + ですか = How is...? (e.g., 'how')

1019
00:47:38,938 --> 00:47:41,974
Listening Test

1020
00:47:41,974 --> 00:47:45,507
It’s perfect.

1021
00:47:45,507 --> 00:47:50,407
ぴったり = Perfect fit!

1022
00:47:50,430 --> 00:47:52,904
Listening Test

1023
00:47:52,904 --> 00:47:55,738
Great!

1024
00:47:59,694 --> 00:48:03,327
Listening Test

1025
00:48:03,327 --> 00:48:07,596
Do you have this in other colors?

1026
00:48:07,596 --> 00:48:13,430
N + は + ありますか = Do you have N? (e.g., 'different color')

1027
00:48:13,453 --> 00:48:16,523
Listening Test

1028
00:48:16,523 --> 00:48:20,090
We have it in black and white.

1029
00:48:20,090 --> 00:48:25,023
N1 + と + N2 = N1 and N2 (e.g., 'black' and 'white')

1030
00:48:25,046 --> 00:48:28,000
Listening Test

1031
00:48:28,000 --> 00:48:31,434
Can I see the black one?

1032
00:48:31,434 --> 00:48:36,167
Vて + ください = Please... (e.g., 'show me')

1033
00:48:36,190 --> 00:48:38,890
Listening Test

1034
00:48:38,890 --> 00:48:41,990
Certainly.

1035
00:48:46,292 --> 00:48:49,476
Listening Test

1036
00:48:49,476 --> 00:48:53,189
Which one do you prefer?

1037
00:48:53,189 --> 00:48:58,289
どちら + が + いいですか = Which one is better? (e.g., 'which one')

1038
00:48:58,312 --> 00:49:02,045
Listening Test

1039
00:49:02,045 --> 00:49:06,479
Black really suits you.

1040
00:49:06,479 --> 00:49:12,478
N + が + お似(に)合(あ)いです = N suits you (e.g., 'customer')

1041
00:49:12,501 --> 00:49:14,934
Listening Test

1042
00:49:14,934 --> 00:49:17,691
You think so?

1043
00:49:21,581 --> 00:49:23,614
Yes?

1044
00:49:23,637 --> 00:49:26,827
Listening Test

1045
00:49:26,827 --> 00:49:30,561
I’ll go with the black one, then.

1046
00:49:30,561 --> 00:49:35,703
N + に + します = I’ll decide on N

1047
00:49:35,727 --> 00:49:37,960
Listening Test

1048
00:49:37,960 --> 00:49:40,462
Thanks!

1049
00:49:43,996 --> 00:49:47,376
Listening Test

1050
00:49:47,376 --> 00:49:51,328
Can I pay with a credit card?

1051
00:49:51,328 --> 00:49:56,763
V (potential form) + ますか = Can you...? (e.g., 'credit card')

1052
00:49:56,787 --> 00:49:58,854
Yes?

1053
00:49:58,877 --> 00:50:00,989
Listening Test

1054
00:50:00,989 --> 00:50:03,356
Please do.

1055
00:50:06,712 --> 00:50:09,712
Listening Test

1056
00:50:09,712 --> 00:50:13,181
Certainly.

1057
00:50:17,990 --> 00:50:19,490
Scene 7: Checking the Document Together

1058
00:50:19,490 --> 00:50:22,074
Um...

1059
00:50:22,097 --> 00:50:23,764
Yes?

1060
00:50:23,787 --> 00:50:27,654
Listening Test

1061
00:50:27,654 --> 00:50:32,191
Can I take a look at that document?

1062
00:50:32,191 --> 00:50:38,424
Vて + もらえる？ = Can you do... for me? (e.g., 'document')

1063
00:50:38,447 --> 00:50:41,033
Listening Test

1064
00:50:41,033 --> 00:50:44,000
This one?

1065
00:50:44,000 --> 00:50:48,136
N + ですか？ = Is it N?

1066
00:50:48,159 --> 00:50:50,461
Yep.

1067
00:50:50,484 --> 00:50:52,718
Here you go.

1068
00:50:52,741 --> 00:50:54,849
Listening Test

1069
00:50:54,849 --> 00:50:57,208
Thanks.

1070
00:51:00,546 --> 00:51:03,846
Listening Test

1071
00:51:03,846 --> 00:51:07,713
It's tough, isn't it?

1072
00:51:07,713 --> 00:51:13,017
いA + ですよね = It’s..., right? (e.g., 'difficult' vs. 'easy')

1073
00:51:13,040 --> 00:51:16,216
Listening Test

1074
00:51:16,216 --> 00:51:19,917
Really tough.

1075
00:51:19,917 --> 00:51:25,017
すごく = Very / Really (e.g., 'difficult')

1076
00:51:25,040 --> 00:51:28,110
Listening Test

1077
00:51:28,110 --> 00:51:31,677
What part don’t you understand?

1078
00:51:31,677 --> 00:51:36,594
どこ + が + Vない + んですか？ = Where is it that you don’t...? (e.g., 'understand')

1079
00:51:36,617 --> 00:51:39,591
Listening Test

1080
00:51:39,591 --> 00:51:43,058
It’s this number.

1081
00:51:43,058 --> 00:51:47,829
N + だよ = It’s N (e.g., 'number')

1082
00:51:47,853 --> 00:51:50,986
Listening Test

1083
00:51:50,986 --> 00:51:54,653
Oh, that one?

1084
00:51:59,710 --> 00:52:02,543
Listening Test

1085
00:52:02,543 --> 00:52:05,810
Isn’t that wrong?

1086
00:52:05,810 --> 00:52:10,345
Vて + ない？ = Isn’t it...? (e.g., 'wrong')

1087
00:52:10,368 --> 00:52:13,314
Listening Test

1088
00:52:13,314 --> 00:52:16,747
Let me check.

1089
00:52:16,747 --> 00:52:21,481
Vます + ね = I’ll... (e.g., 'confirm')

1090
00:52:21,504 --> 00:52:23,660
Thanks.

1091
00:52:23,683 --> 00:52:26,483
Listening Test

1092
00:52:26,483 --> 00:52:29,721
You’re right.

1093
00:52:29,721 --> 00:52:34,221
なA + ですね = It really is..., isn’t it? (e.g., 'true')

1094
00:52:34,244 --> 00:52:38,482
Listening Test

1095
00:52:38,482 --> 00:52:43,517
My bad, that was my mistake.

1096
00:52:43,517 --> 00:52:50,383
やっぱり = As expected / Just as I thought (e.g., 'N’s N' / 'mistake')

1097
00:52:50,406 --> 00:52:53,182
Listening Test

1098
00:52:53,182 --> 00:52:56,379
Please fix it.

1099
00:52:56,379 --> 00:53:00,846
Vて + おいてね = Please do... in advance (e.g., 'fix')

1100
00:53:00,869 --> 00:53:02,803
Yes?

1101
00:53:02,825 --> 00:53:06,299
Listening Test

1102
00:53:06,299 --> 00:53:10,374
The meeting starts at three.

1103
00:53:10,374 --> 00:53:15,972
N + から + だよ = It’s from N (e.g., 'meeting')

1104
00:53:15,995 --> 00:53:18,428
Listening Test

1105
00:53:18,428 --> 00:53:21,166
I’ll make it in time.

1106
00:53:21,166 --> 00:53:25,000
間(ま)に合(あ)わせます = I’ll make it in time!

1107
00:53:25,023 --> 00:53:28,089
Listening Test

1108
00:53:28,089 --> 00:53:31,638
Could you also make copies?

1109
00:53:31,638 --> 00:53:36,539
N + も + お願(ねが)いね = Please do N too (e.g., 'copy')

1110
00:53:36,563 --> 00:53:38,829
Listening Test

1111
00:53:38,829 --> 00:53:41,379
How many copies?

1112
00:53:41,379 --> 00:53:44,935
何(なん) + counter + ですか？ = How many...? (e.g., 'copies')

1113
00:53:44,958 --> 00:53:47,658
Listening Test

1114
